    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d560">

                <pb facs="0615" n="565" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg565"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Baker to Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-06-15"><hi rendition="#italic">June 15,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I am in receipt of the following telegram
                    from Salvador: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p rendition="#right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">San Salvador</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">3:15 p.m., May 15, 1894.</hi><lb/><hi
                                rendition="#small-caps">Managua</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">6
                                p.m., May 15, 1894</hi>.</p>
                        <p rendition="#flush">Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Baker</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Minister Plenipotentiary of the United States,
                                Managua:</hi></p>
                        <p>I have the honor of communicating to you that the Government of the
                            United States has recognized, by cable, Gen. Rafael A. Gutierrez as
                            President of this Republic. As the President’s general secretary I
                            solicit in the name of justice the extradition of Antonio Ezeta and his
                            companions who have found an asylum on the U. S. S. <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Bennington</hi> at the port of La Libertad. The
                            said criminals are accused of and prosecuted for the common crimes of
                            murder, robbery, arson, and other atrocities. I beg your excellency to
                            accept the considerations with which I subscribe myself your obedient
                            servant.</p>
                        <p rendition="#right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Estanislao
                                Perez</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Minister-General.</hi></p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>No answer was made to this, awaiting instructions from Washington.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lewis Baker.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
